{"name":"UK public contract records for multi-year NovaSeq 6000 support plans (ukspending.com and Contracts Finder)","url":"https://ukspending.com/contracts/50927","access":"I opened this page. University of Birmingham bought a £589,058 Illumina Silver support contract covering MiSeq, NextSeq500/2000 and the NovaSeq 6000, running 8 Sep 2025 to 7 Sep 2029 (published 6 Jan 2025). A second notice, https://www.contractsfinder.service.gov.uk/Notice/2b3405cc-ee07-410c-a3b2-17114c293cd9, returned 403 to the fetch tool; the search snippet shows £119,360.40 of NovaSeq 6000 maintenance from 18 Jan 2026 to 17 Jan 2027, bought as a framework call-off. Next steps: on ukspending.com, search 'NovaSeq 6000', 'NovaSeq 6000Dx', 'Illumina support plan' and 'NovaSeq X'. On Contracts Finder, search the same terms for 2025-26 (try archive.ph if it returns 403). For each record, note the buyer (NHS Genomic Lab Hub or university), the term end date, and whether the instrument is the 6000 or the X.","labels":["1A"],"rationale":"These records test whether the 6000 tail is permanent or migrating. Multi-year support bought after 2025 that runs to 2027-2029 is hard evidence that owners plan to keep the 6000 for years, which cuts against a 5-point 2027 shift. Contracts that end in 2026-27 with no renewal, or that are replaced by X service contracts, support migration. Taken together, term end dates give an independent clock for when the UK clinical and academic tail runs out.","expected_payoff":"high"},
