{"name":"FDA AccessGUDID and EUDAMED device records for NovaSeq 6000Dx reagents vs any NovaSeq X Dx registration","url":"https://beudamed.com/fda_udis/00816270020637","access":"Seen in search (beudamed and revmedconnect pages for NovaSeq 6000Dx, UDI 00816270020637); not opened. My call to the AccessGUDID API at /api/v3/devices/search.json returned 404. Use https://accessgudid.nlm.nih.gov/devices/search?query=NovaSeq in the HTML view, or the openFDA device UDI endpoint: https://api.fda.gov/device/udi.json?search=brand_name:NovaSeq&limit=100. Record each UDI's brand, version, publish date and revision date. Then check whether any 'NovaSeq X' IVD or Dx record exists, and whether new 6000Dx reagent versions were registered in 2025-26.","labels":["1A"],"rationale":"Illumina has no NovaSeq X Dx; my search found only the 6000Dx, which is IVDR Class A. If Illumina is still registering or revising 6000Dx consumable records in 2025-26 and has filed nothing for an X Dx, the regulated clinical tail has no legal destination before 2027. That supports the watch-out that the tail is sticky, while also showing where a future Dx launch would trigger migration. This is a different source from S215 (PMA supplements) and S148 (the IVDR web page).","expected_payoff":"medium"},
